{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 1"},"body":"The captured configured assertion and the cited paper assertion were read with their relevant definitions; the disclosed relation follows the stated scope, not the previous frontend choice.\n\nInspected: Read all three configured declarations and MainConclusion/CriticalLawsConclusion, including the simultaneous uniform-edge coupling and critical-tail exponents.\n\nEditorial revision by Codex, 26 October 2026: wording and display metadata clarified; pinned source texts and proposed relations unchanged. No human review or proof replay was added.\n\nCapture rebinding by Codex, 26 October 2026: the Atlas capture revision changed after an outside-report wording correction. The pinned Lean text, configuration, paper text and proposed relation are unchanged; no new review is implied.","content_sha256":"sha256:03907e94581d2d3e36e6932eaf68e6947fdda241a5dfa3dbda9b3dbf137fc519","fingerprint":"sha256:3b95e77acb933f2e4318593cf8a0d7a28241c865c8f8758f4e27a2e77c6a5447","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. The captured configured assertion and the cited paper assertion were read with their relevant definitions; the disclosed relation follows the stated scope, not the previous frontend choice.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:1751e2795328a58a27f29568bf993f63c29cfeb82d87a80d87038e2428a67a47","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.Percolation.BenjaminiSchramm.full_main"],"explanation":"For infinite connected locally finite quasi-transitive graphs with positive vertex expansion, both assert that the critical connection operator norm equals the supremum below criticality and is finite, with pc<p2≤pu. Both also assert an interval on which infinitely many infinite clusters exist simultaneously almost surely in the uniform-edge coupling.","fingerprint":"sha256:13f8dd02e2a5b90eb6275bfc10015ce31c2abbe2097f753efffbf35a4245a92d","general_disclaimer":true,"limitations":"Source-level formulation comparison only; this is not independent verification of the definitions, Lean proof, or manuscript proof.","relation":"same-claim","row_id":"Nonuniqueness-of-percolation-on-nonamenable-quasi-transitive-graphs-September-24-2026#thm:main","statement_sha256":"sha256:24c825930f799150daf30887a4018f1734983e7093606c6d68dc2db93284bb4c"},{"declarations":["OAI.Percolation.BenjaminiSchramm.cayley_main"],"explanation":"Both formulations apply to every finite symmetric identity-free generating set of a nonamenable finitely generated group. They include the critical operator and nonuniqueness conclusions, and infinitely many infinite clusters almost surely at each fixed p strictly between pc and pu.","fingerprint":"sha256:fae39cd0e0a44f94c50756da82a11f62752905f59ac65730e8f78474ad925a1a","general_disclaimer":true,"limitations":"Source-level formulation comparison only; this is not independent verification of the definitions, Lean proof, or manuscript proof.","relation":"same-claim","row_id":"Nonuniqueness-of-percolation-on-nonamenable-quasi-transitive-graphs-September-24-2026#cor:cayley","statement_sha256":"sha256:75d1d1a4aedb5c2904d2595781945bf310d83b27674f2f23c8497f949a4558a8"},{"declarations":["OAI.Percolation.BenjaminiSchramm.critical_laws"],"explanation":"The critical-laws declaration matches the finite triangle diagram, susceptibility and percolation exponents, volume-tail exponent 1/2 and intrinsic/extrinsic radius-tail exponent 1. It also retains pc<p2≤pexp and exponential connection decay at each parameter below p2, as the paper’s corollary states.","fingerprint":"sha256:d8cbf290aee40aa37ef020f72459a89d989915a48a7